WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.013
Unit 2 starts with how a
group reaches the engine.

2
00:00:03.013 --> 00:00:06.285
An Entra group reaches Sequel
Server as a group login,

3
00:00:06.285 --> 00:00:08.475
then a database user added to a role.

4
00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:11.235
The data platform book's
Chapter 16, Groups,

5
00:00:11.235 --> 00:00:15.650
Roles and How Membership Reaches
the Engine, makes one rule central.

6
00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:19.169
Each Entra group grants exactly
one role, on one database,

7
00:00:19.169 --> 00:00:22.687
in one environment, so the
group's name says what it grants.

8
00:00:22.687 --> 00:00:26.640
The model stays flat, because
dynamic groups can't contain groups,

9
00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:31.250
and nesting builds on behavior that is
unsupported, ending or undocumented.

10
00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:34.750
Members are listed directly,
by rule or by assignment.

11
00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:38.217
One group, one role is checked
where the roles are known:

12
00:00:38.217 --> 00:00:40.375
the login plan from Module 4 warns.

13
00:00:40.375 --> 00:00:42.854
The group map carries grants per instance,

14
00:00:42.854 --> 00:00:45.910
not roles per database, so
it doesn't repeat the check.
